= K-163 recovery transfer and horizontal control
_Formal gates, not a weakness result_ · 2026-10-31

*Outcome.* Let
`r = 5846006549323611672814741753598448348329118574063`. The compiled Lean
module checks `gcd(45641, r) = 1`. A generic theorem proves that additive maps
with `recovery(phi(X)) = [45641]X` make `phi` injective on `r`-torsion,
preserve exact point order, and preserve and reflect scalar relations.

`[r]Q=0` says only that `Q` is `r`-torsion. Calling the scalar-relation
equivalence a discrete-log result requires a separate proof that `Q` belongs
to the cyclic subgroup generated by the base `P`.

A stronger same-curve control defines

#align(center)[`alpha = 51 - 160 tau`,  `alpha_bar = -109 + 160 tau`]

and derives both compositions `[45641]` from `tau^2 = tau - 2`. This proves no
vertical map, vertical dual, concrete Frobenius bridge, speedup, attack, or
weak curve. Both named targets compile and pass requested-theorem axiom
audits. The repository-wide receipt remains pending because an unrelated
pre-existing Semaev certificate exceeded local memory.

